  "sortOrder": 19007,
  "verseCount": 17,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "O LORD my God, in thee do I put my trust: save me from all them that persecute me, and deliver me:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Lest he tear my soul like a lion, rending it in pieces, while there is none to deliver.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "O LORD my God, if I have done this; if there be iniquity in my hands;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "If I have rewarded evil unto him that was at peace with me; (yea, I have delivered him that without cause is mine enemy:)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Let the enemy persecute my soul, and take it; yea, let him tread down my life upon the earth, and lay mine honour in the dust. Selah.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Arise, O LORD, in thine anger, lift up thyself because of the rage of mine enemies: and awake for me to the judgment that thou hast commanded.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "So shall the congregation of the people compass thee about: for their sakes therefore return thou on high.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "The LORD shall judge the people: judge me, O LORD, according to my righteousness, and according to mine integrity that is in me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end; but establish the just: for the righteous God trieth the hearts and reins.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "My defence is of God, which saveth the upright in heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "God judgeth the righteous, and God is angry with the wicked every day.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "If he turn not, he will whet his sword; he hath bent his bow, and made it ready.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "He hath also prepared for him the instruments of death; he ordaineth his arrows against the persecutors.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Behold, he travaileth with iniquity, and hath conceived mischief, and brought forth falsehood.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "He made a pit, and digged it, and is fallen into the ditch which he made.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "His mischief shall return upon his own head, and his violent dealing shall come down upon his own pate.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:7:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "I will praise the LORD according to his righteousness: and will sing praise to the name of the LORD most high.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 7:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:7:17"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
